   "type": "DOCUMENT",
   "isFreePreview": true,
   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">JSC301m · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 13947 · Decision 1363/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 06/12/2024 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">JSC301m · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 13947 · QĐ 1363/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 06/12/2024 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>・Attend at least 80% of in-class hours to qualify for the final exam.<br>・Read the textbook and present their understanding of assigned contents (in Japanese) in groups.<br>・Practice research by exploring issues related to Japanese culture, society, and people (with possible comparisons to Vietnam).<br>・Review lecture content, compare with instructor-provided materials and slides to firmly grasp knowledge and vocabulary related to Japanese culture and society.<br>・Actively participate in class discussions on given topics.<br>・Students may use AI (ChatGPT, Copilot, etc.) to improve learning effectiveness. AI can be applied specifically in the following areas:<br>1. Vocabulary: use AI to look up meanings of Japanese words and how they are used in context.<br>2. Knowledge of culture, society, and history: use AI to research information and terminology in reading passages related to the course topics, as well as in preparing presentations.<br>3. Review for Small Tests and Final Exam: use AI to systematically review learned content in a clear and scientific way.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>・Attend at least 80% of in-class hours to qualify for the final exam.<br>・Read the textbook and present their understanding of assigned contents (in Japanese) in groups.<br>・Practice research by exploring issues related to Japanese culture, society, and people (with possible comparisons to Vietnam).<br>・Review lecture content, compare with instructor-provided materials and slides to firmly grasp knowledge and vocabulary related to Japanese culture and society.<br>・Actively participate in class discussions on given topics.<br>・Students may use AI (ChatGPT, Copilot, etc.) to improve learning effectiveness. AI can be applied specifically in the following areas:<br>1. Vocabulary: use AI to look up meanings of Japanese words and how they are used in context.<br>2. Knowledge of culture, society, and history: use AI to research information and terminology in reading passages related to the course topics, as well as in preparing presentations.<br>3. Review for Small Tests and Final Exam: use AI to systematically review learned content in a clear and scientific way.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13947\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13947</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13947\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13947</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
